                            1  An Introduction
                            ==================

     This program is a WWIV look-alike program.  WWIV is a popular BBS
program available for MS-DOS Compatibles and a look-alike (Hermes) is
available for the Mac.  I decided to make a good utility which is available
for other computer platforms available for the Amiga.
     Stellar BBS is written in 100% SAS/C 5.10 code.  You shouldn't
experience many problems while multitasking, as you would with compiled
BASIC or something similar.
     Stellar BBS is not complete.  Although it does contain many features,
there are still a lot more features to be added.  If there is a demand for
this program to be updated, I will do so.  There is no need to work on a
program for no reason.
     The documentation is also incomplete at the moment.  I just don't like
writing documentation very much.  Expect complete docs by the 1.00 release.
Additional documentation can be had by getting a hold of the WWIV user
manual.  It may not be exactly the same, but it should you the same idea on
what certain commands do.
     Stellar BBS is a shareware product.  You are provided with a "crippled"
version of the program.  Only a maximum of 3 users may have an account with
the crippled version.  To receive the real thing, a registration fee of $30
is required.  I'll send you the latest version along with a program called
